--TEST--
`Core\Response\Stream::write` sends octets no text-shaped chunk could carry, and a body written in chunks is byte-for-byte the body written whole -- `rule:concurrency/a-stream-that-outlives-its-request-is-a-connection` and `rule:types/bytes`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Response\Stream::write
// The `bytes` arm of the one parameter, asked the question `text` cannot be
// asked: a chunk holding a NUL and bytes that are not valid UTF-8 goes out
// unchanged and unmeasured. It is read back through a capture and re-hexed,
// because the bytes themselves are not something an exact expectation can
// spell.
var $sent = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    var $image = Core\Response::stream("image/png");
    $image->write(Core\Encoding::fromHex("89504e470d0a1a0a"));
    $image->write(Core\Encoding::fromHex("00ff"));
});
echo Core\Encoding::toHex($sent as string as bytes), "\n";

// Agreement, which is the claim a member answering plausibly on its own line
// would still fail: the same body written whole and written in pieces is the
// same bytes. The two members differ in *when* the bytes go out and in nothing
// else, so a stream that dropped, reordered or padded a chunk fails here while
// each half still reads correctly alone.
var $whole = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    Core\Response::text("id,name\n1,ada\n2,alan\n");
});
var $chunked = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    var $rows = Core\Response::stream("text/plain; charset=utf-8");
    $rows->write("id,name\n");
    $rows->write("1,ada\n");
    $rows->write("2,alan\n");
});
if (($whole as string) == ($chunked as string)) {
    echo "agree\n";
} else {
    echo "differ\n";
}
--EXPECT--
89504e470d0a1a0a00ff
agree
